note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note gpu/nvidia/checks/nmm.om: the matmul() block of CUDApp tests/api_attn_rest_diff.c. The units mm_init, mm_dot,
note mm_err and mm_next (gpu/nvidia/om/api/, over ar_dot and ar_err of attn_oracle.om) are the host matmul oracle
note of src/omega_gpu_matmul_api.c; the check drives them with that file's loop (ported in nmrun) and compares the
note result with the pending C oracle (CUDAPP_MIGRATION_PENDING_C_MATMUL_ORACLE_GUARD) the table holds. Here
note mm_init and mm_next are the stand-ins nmm-init.om and nmm-next.om (see there); the units themselves are
note proven by nmmq.om. Rows:
note   M m k n A B C ABS REL MISM PAR
note                  A (m x k) and B (k x n) bfloat16 as 4 hex digits each and C (m x n) float bits as 8 hex
note                  digits each, - when empty; the C oracle answered max_abs_err and max_rel_err (float bits,
note                  8 hex digits), mismatch_count and parity_verified. The units must give the same bits.
note   Z K ABS REL MISM PAR
note                  1 x K x 1 with A all 1.0 and B alternating -1.0, 1.0: a dot product of K terms, past the
note                  1000000-term segment of ar_dot when K is larger; built here, not read from the table.
note The kept operands live in arrays of 4096 values (A, B and C each); a larger row is refused as malformed
note (ckbad, exit 2), never cut. Z rows hold at most 1000003 terms, two arrays of that many bfloat16 in nmz.
text t_name "NMM"
fn cname to void
for i ulong len t_name bound 64
ckoc ulong get t_name i
end
end
note value j of hex field i, w bytes wide, as printed (most significant first)
fn nmh i ulong j ulong w ulong to ulong
v = ulong 0
for x ulong w bound 8
v = or shl v 8 ckhex i add mul j w x
end
ret v
end
note one dot product of the loop; true when mm_dot answered 0, as the C loop requires. p is q[0..4) (the C passes
note q with length 4).
fn nmdot a view ushort * b view ushort * q view ulong 8 d edit ulong 2 to bool
p = new ulong 4 0
for i ulong 4
put p i get q i
end
ret eq mm_dot part a 0 get q 6 part b 0 get q 7 p d 0
end
note the oracle loop of src/omega_gpu_matmul_api.c, q = {0, 0, k, n, m, 0, 0, 0}, z = {0, 0, 0, 1}. w holds m, k, n
note in slots 0 to 2 (one array: a function has six parameter slots and an unsized view takes two); z, the
note answer (max_abs_err, max_rel_err, mismatch_count, parity_verified), is copied to slots 4 to 7; slot 3 holds r,
note the loop's go-on flag.
fn nmerr d view ulong 2 c view uint 4096 q view ulong 8 z edit ulong 4 to bool
ret eq mm_err d get c get q 5 z 0
end
fn nmrun a view ushort * b view ushort * c view uint 4096 w edit ulong 8 to bool
q = new ulong 8 0
d = new ulong 2 0
z = new ulong 4 0
put q 2 get w 1
put q 3 get w 2
put q 4 get w 0
put z 3 1
put w 3 0
if mm_init q
put w 3 1
end
for it ulong mul get w 0 get w 2 bound 4096
if eq get w 3 0
ret false
end
if not nmdot a b q d
ret false
end
if not nmerr d c q z
ret false
end
put w 3 0
if mm_next q
put w 3 1
end
end
for i ulong 4
put w add i 4 get z i
end
ret eq get w 3 0
end
fn nmfill i ulong w ulong cnt ulong o edit ushort 4096 to void
if eq cnt 0
if ne ckhexn i 0
ckbad
end
ret
end
if ne ckhexn i mul cnt w
ckbad
end
for j ulong cnt bound 4096
put o j ushort nmh i j w
end
end
fn nmfillc cnt ulong o edit uint 4096 to void
if eq cnt 0
if ne ckhexn 6 0
ckbad
end
ret
end
if ne ckhexn 6 mul cnt 4
ckbad
end
for j ulong cnt bound 4096
put o j uint nmh 6 j 4
end
end
fn nmok w view ulong 8 ia ulong to bool
if ne get w 4 nmh ia 0 4
ret false
end
if ne get w 5 nmh add ia 1 0 4
ret false
end
if ne get w 6 cknum add ia 2
ret false
end
ret eq get w 7 cknum add ia 3
end
fn nmz to bool
la = new ushort 1000003 0
lb = new ushort 1000003 0
lc = new uint 4096 0
w = new ulong 8 1
if ne ckcnt 6
ckbad
end
kk = cknum 1
if or eq kk 0 gt kk 1000003
ckbad
end
if or ne ckhexn 2 4 ne ckhexn 3 4
ckbad
end
for i ulong kk bound 1000003
put la i ushort 16256
if eq and i 1 0
put lb i ushort 49024
else
put lb i ushort 16256
end
end
put lc 0 uint 1065353216
put w 1 kk
if not nmrun part la 0 kk part lb 0 kk lc w
ret false
end
ret nmok w 2
end
note the shape m, k, n of an M row into w slots 0 to 2; a shape whose operands pass 4096 values is refused
fn nmshape w edit ulong 8 to void
for i ulong 3
v = cknum add i 1
if gt v 4096
ckbad
end
put w i v
end
if gt mul get w 0 get w 1 4096
ckbad
end
if gt mul get w 1 get w 2 4096
ckbad
end
if gt mul get w 0 get w 2 4096
ckbad
end
if or ne ckhexn 7 4 ne ckhexn 8 4
ckbad
end
end
fn crow to bool
a = new ushort 4096 0
b = new ushort 4096 0
c = new uint 4096 0
w = new ulong 8 0
if ne cklen 0 1
ckbad
end
k0 = ckch 0 0
if eq k0 90
ret nmz
end
if or ne k0 77 ne ckcnt 11
ckbad
end
nmshape w
nmfill 4 2 mul get w 0 get w 1 a
nmfill 5 2 mul get w 1 get w 2 b
nmfillc mul get w 0 get w 2 c
if not nmrun a b c w
ret false
end
ret nmok w 7
end
